From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:48:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 05/39] Review fixes: Debye hooks, probe end arming, setup
 cache key, portability (snapshot cg17)

Found by an independent read-only correctness review of the fork (2026-11-02):

- Engine_Ext_DebyeMaterial lost its dispersion in the multithreaded engine: it inherited
  Engine_Ext_Dispersive::GetUsedHooks() (APPLY_VOLT | LINE_HOOKS), so the hook plan never called its
  DoPre/PostVoltageUpdates and Debye cells ran as their base material (the single-threaded engines were
  right; 37 % of the peak field on a 60x60x20 Debye box after 600 steps). It now declares
  PRE_VOLT | POST_VOLT | APPLY_VOLT and no line hooks (the fused sweep stays off with it). Structural
  guard: OPENEMS_HOOKS_DECLARED_BY(Class) at the start of every GetUsedHooks() override returns
  LEGACY_HOOKS for any subclass that does not override it itself, so a declaration can never be
  inherited again. Engine_Ext_Dispersive::DispersiveHooks() is the non-virtual base set for subclasses.
- Probe end criterion (OPENEMS_PROBE_END_DB): a probe the wavefront had not reached yet (peak still 0)
  counted as settled, so a model with a one-way delay longer than the hold could stop before its far
  port saw the pulse. The hold now starts only once every probe has a non-zero peak; a non-Gaussian
  excitation with the knob set prints a notice instead of being ignored silently.
- Operator::GetMaterial(): the per-thread last-lookup cache is keyed by a setup generation
  (bumped in CalcECOperator) so a later setup in the same process can never reuse a pointer to a
  freed property of an earlier one.
- Engine_Ext_Excitation declares APPLY_CURR only when it has current excitations (one barrier per
  timestep less for the usual voltage excitation).
- Auto thread tuner: never queues more threads than x-lines (it timed the clamped count repeatedly).
- nf2ff: the separable (BLAS) path is used only when a CBLAS is available (Apple Accelerate); other
  builds keep the threaded legacy loop instead of a single-threaded scalar fallback.
- Packed coefficient tables are skipped (SoA tables, generic loops) when they would exceed twice the
  field memory or allocation fails, instead of aborting the setup.
- Cleanups: SetupTimer below the includes in operator.cpp, unused includes in
  operator_sse_compressed.cpp, the NX-1 current-hook invariant documented in engine_extension.h.

Verified: Debye box bit-identical across basic / sse-compressed / multithreaded engines (the single
engine unchanged against cg16); the six bench models bit-identical to stock v0.37.0 at 4, 8 and auto
threads (results/*_cg17.txt); CylindricalWave_CC multigrid 18 HDF5 datasets 0 differences; GCPW probe
end stops at the same step (45570) with a bit-identical port-file prefix.

